    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d979">

                <pb facs="1118" n="1022" xml:id="pg1022"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr. Woodford.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-03-11"><hi rendition="#italic">March 11,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 158.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 158, of the 25th ultimo, quoting the remarks made by you at the dinner which
                    you gave to Señor Polo de Barnabé, the recently appointed minister from Spain to
                    the United States. They are cordially approved by this Government.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
